   9:     Fill the rectangle from the lone foreground pixel to its nearest grid corner.
  10: 
  11:     Input structure
  12:     - The grid is a uniform background field with exactly one foreground pixel.
  13:     - The foreground pixel's color is the color used for all added pixels.
  14: 
  15:     Rule
  16:     - Find the grid corner with the smallest Manhattan distance to the foreground pixel.
  17:     - Recolor every pixel in the inclusive axis-aligned rectangle bounded by that
  18:       corner and the foreground pixel to the foreground color.
  19: 
  20:     Key insight
  21:     - The single pixel is one corner of the rectangle; the opposite corner is the
  22:       nearest corner of the whole canvas.
  23:     """
  24:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  25:     bg = get_bg(g)
  26:     foreground = np.argwhere(g != bg)
